osx-gpu: radeonsi on a big-endian host, part three: indexed draws, queries, and buffer clears

1. VGT_INDEX_TYPE (si_state_draw.cpp): V_028A7C_VGT_DMA_SWAP_16_BIT (1) and
   V_028A7C_VGT_DMA_SWAP_32_BIT (2) in amdgfxregs.h are unshifted field
   values for S_028A7C_SWAP_MODE [3:2], unlike r600d.h where VGT_DMA_SWAP_*
   already carried (x << 2). ORing them raw into index_type overwrote
   INDEX_TYPE [1:0] (turning u16 into unswapped u32 and u32 into invalid 3),
   causing every glDrawElements call on GFX6-7 big-endian to draw zero pixels.
2. ubyte_to_ushort (si_shaderlib_nir.c): internal shaders skip
   si_nir_lower_be_memory, so widen GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE indices to big-endian
   uint16_t (shifted left by 8) on GFX6-7 big-endian to match
   VGT_DMA_SWAP_16_BIT.
3. Hardware and QBO queries (si_query.c, si_shaderlib_nir.c): the GPU writes
   little-endian query dwords; convert CPU reads/writes and QBO constants/SSBO
   results between little-endian and host byte order.
4. Buffer clears (si_compute_blit.c): byte-swap application host-order clear
   values in si_pipe_clear_buffer before GPU clear while leaving internal
   scalar metadata clears untouched.

